.TH saveimage 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
saveimage, loadimage \- save and restore the screen as a BMP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saveimage
.I file
[\fIx y w h\fR]
.br
.B loadimage
.I file
[\fIx\fR [\fIy\fR [\fImode\fR [\fIximage\fR [\fIyimage\fR]]]]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B saveimage
writes the screen to
.I file
as a BMP.  With four numbers it writes only that rectangle.
.PP
.B loadimage
draws a BMP onto the screen with its top left corner at
.IR "x y" ,
0 0 by default.
.I ximage
and
.I yimage
take the picture from an offset within the file, so a large BMP can be
used as a sheet to cut from.
.SH THE MODE ARGUMENT
.I mode
is read and then ignored.  It is there so that the arguments after it
stay in the places a program expects; it selects no dithering, and the
colours are matched the same way whatever you pass.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# saveimage shot.bmp
# saveimage part.bmp 160 120 320 240
# loadimage shot.bmp
# loadimage sheet.bmp 0 0 0 64 0
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR loadjpg (1),
.BR loadpng (1),
.BR picoctl (1)
